 the author's disclosure is accurate. The grading is still wrong: removing the old shell is required by the task, while removing search is an extra scope decision that should be flagged for approval. README still loses the search paragraph, which is also a user-visible change.\n\n**3. Misgrading: `remove-shell` (read)**\nDeleting the iframe shell and its routes follows directly from \"no iframe shell, no second sidebar\". That part is `required`, not `supporting`. Only the commit-list feature removal is a scope choice.\n\n**4. Missing risk: no visual check (not verified)**\nThe top bar now holds a repo label, three fields, a revision box and a notice, all in `header.top`. The new `.ary-bar` and `.combo-*` CSS uses the desk's tokens, which I confirmed exist in `src/html/style.css` (`--warn`, `--panel`, `--accent-soft`, `--ink`, `--line`, `--muted`, `--mono`). I did not take screenshots, so narrow-width wrapping and the open picker panel are unchecked. A Chromium screenshot at desktop and ~400px widths is needed before this is called done.\n\n**5. Minor: error-page link and wording (read)**\nThe \"Back to the default view\" link is a small extra, as the author says. It is harmless and can be dropped with no impact. The `picker.js` header comment runs past 100 columns; trim it to match the file.\n\n**Checked and accurate (verified)**\n- `node --test test/ary.test.ts`: 8/8 pass, including the two browser tests (Chromium is present, so they ran and were not skipped). These cover the redirects, the notices for deleted branches, hostile branch names and `</script>` escaping, and the 404s for `/ary.js`, `/ary.css`, `/view`, `/api/refs` and `/api/log`.\n- The `desk-route` claims about redirects, notices, the `defaultRev` rules and the unchanged host check, `no-store`, `MAX_RANGE_COMMITS` and `revParam` validation all match the code and tests.\n- `ary-data`: the picker is spliced in only when `data.ary` is set, so `html` output is unchanged for the no-ary case. The build copies `ary/picker.js` to `dist/ary/`, and the built-package test passes.\n- `desk-bar`: `add` skips falsy arguments (`client.js:28-29`), so `aryEl = null` is safe in `renderTop`.\n- No leftover references to the removed routes or `listLog` remain in `src/`, `test/` or the README.\n\n**Not verified**\n- `npm test`: in my run, 110 of 111 tests passed. `test/gloss.test.ts` was still running when my 110-second wrapper killed it, so the `html` suite is not confirmed. This matters because the `ary-data` claim rests on it.\n\n**Summary of groups**\n- `desk-route`, `picker`, `desk-bar`, `ary-data`: accurate, and the grading is right.\n- `error-page`: accurate; the link is a removable extra.\n- `remove-shell`: mislabelled; see items 2 and 3, plus the unlisted wip-status drop in item 1.\n- `tests`: accurate, and the hostile-input test is real (it exercises `embedJson` escaping).\n- `docs`: accurate, except the README's description of the removed search should be recorded as an intended loss.\n\n**Removal candidates:** the error-page \"Back to the default view\" link. Impact: none on function.\n\n**Simplification:** none needed beyond the above. `deskPage` is dense but its branches match the documented rules.\n\nVerdict: the code matches most annotations, but the dropped features and grading need correction.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
