-gloss.js`. I did not load the pages in a headless browser, so the layout and picker claims rest on reading and the author's tests.\n\n### Findings, most important first\n\n1. **Mismatch (verified).** The base picker's \"(none: all of the branch's history)\" option does not show the branch's history. `go(head, null, null)` sends `/?head=feat`, and `defaultRev` then picks the newest commit only. I ran it in a three-commit repo with a one-commit feature branch: `/?head=feat` returned 302 to `?rev=<tip>`, and the page had `range: null` with one commit. The same happens for the deleted-base notice, \"showing all of feat's history\", which also renders one commit. This is in `desk-route` and `desk-bar`. The browser test only checks the label text, not the list. The README sentence \"The desk's own sidebar then lists the commits of that range\" is also wrong for this case. The fix is either to make \"none\" produce a whole-history rev, or to change the label and notice text.\n\n2. **Missing risk, dead end (verified).** In a repo with no local branches and a detached HEAD, `GET /` returns 422 \"there are no branches to show\". The page has no pickers, and its \"Back to the default view\" link goes to `/`, which returns the same error. The only way out is to type `?rev=` into the URL by hand. The author lists \"an error page without pickers\" as a risk but not that the escape link loops. This is in `error-page` and `desk-route`. Possible fixes: fall back to `rev=HEAD` when it resolves, or render the pickers even with no head.\n\n3. **Misgrading: `error-page` (read).** The \"Back to the default view\" link is an extra the author says they added. In the case above it loops, so it is a removal candidate, or it should be dropped in favour of a plain message.\n\n4. **Misgrading: `sticky-bar` (read).** It is labelled supporting, but the task does not need it. It changes the `html` page too, which the summary describes as \"unchanged\" apart from the top bar. The author notes the same rail bug exists in `html`. Keeping it is defensible because the taller ary bar would otherwise hide the rail. It should be graded as an incidental fix bundled into the task, with the `html` change named as a user-visible change. Removal impact: the rail's last rows are unreachable at scroll 0 on wide screens in ary. The `ResizeObserver` could be dropped if the bar's height is fixed, but the bar wraps, so it probably stays.\n\n5. **Test gap (read).** No test checks what the \"(none)\" choice lists, which is why finding 1 passed. A test asserting that `?head=main&base=` lists the history would catch it.\n\n6. **Minor (read).** `aryBar` and `picker.js` add a global `function aryBar` to the nonce'd script, and a `mousedown` listener on `document` that is never removed. Harmless for a single-page desk. `defaultRev` runs `rev-list --count` on every `/` request, which walks the full base..head range; that is acceptable under the 200-commit cap.\n\nEverything else I checked matches the annotations: the `required` desk-route and picker groups, the `ary-data` embedding (`data.ary` only), the removal of `/view`, `/api/*` and the old assets, the `html` picker injection path, and the hostile-input and redirect tests.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
