aryBar` could take them as arguments, `aryBar(ary, el, add)`, and the call site `aryBar(data.ary, el, add)` is in the same file as the helpers. That removes about 10 duplicated lines from a script that is spliced into the same `<script>` as `client.js`. It is a small change, and the rendered page should be unaffected.\n\n3. **`known` set built twice** (`src/ary/server.ts`, `deskPage`; `src/ary/browse.ts`, `listRefs`). `listRefs` already builds `names = new Set([...branches, ...remotes])` to find `defaultBase`, and `deskPage` builds the same set again. Returning it from `listRefs` as a `names` field, or exposing a small `isKnownRef`, avoids the second construction. It is a one-line saving, so do it only if you touch these files anyway.\n\n4. **Error page markup inline in `createAry`** (group `error-page`, h12). The line holding the full HTML string and the CSP header is very long. Move it into a small `errorPage(message)` helper beside `PAGE_HEADERS`. `createAry`'s catch block then reads clearly, and the 'no frame, escaped' policy lives next to `PAGE_HEADERS`. It is a pure move of about 3 lines.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
