n this path it only reloads the error.\n\n**Misgraded necessity**\n\n3. **`remove-shell` [supporting] is mislabelled (read).** Deleting the shell, `/view`, `/api/refs` and `/api/log` is the task itself (\"one document, no iframe shell, no second sidebar\"). Its `serves: desk-route` understates that. Its own notes also mix a necessary deletion (the shell and its routes) with a product drop (commit search, Load more, the marks list). The drop decisions are the real judgement calls and deserve their own group.\n\n4. **`tests` [supporting] claims \"(checked)\" for the escaping mutation, which I did not re-run.** The suite passes (see below), but the mutation check itself is unverified.\n\n**Removal candidates**\n\n5. None of the groups are clearly removable. The \"Back to the default view\" link in `error-page` is the only small extra, and it is cheap to drop.\n\n**Simplifications**\n\n6. **`defaultRev` counts an unbounded range (read).** `git rev-list --count base..head` walks the whole range just to compare against 200. Using `--max-count=MAX_RANGE_COMMITS+1` and counting the lines would cap the work. This is minor, since the call only runs on the default view.\n\n7. **The \"base defaults to the default branch unless head is the default\" rule is repeated** in `deskPage` (`baseFor`) and in `picker.js` (`name === ary.defaultBase ? null : ary.defaultBase`). Sending the default base in the data, or computing it once in `deskPage`, would remove the duplication. Low priority.\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n8. **Capability loss is only partly recorded (read).** The old shell let you pick any single commit of a range over 200 commits, and let you search commits by message or author on a large history. Both are gone. The TODO covers the first. The second is only in the summary, not in the author's risk list. Users of big repos now need to know a SHA to reach an old commit.\n\n9. **`/` now does git work on every request** (`listRefs` plus `defaultRev`, which also calls `rev-list`), where the old shell fetched refs and the log lazily. This is fine for a local tool, but it is not listed.\n\nVerified by running: `tsc --noEmit` exits 0. `node --test test/ary.test.ts` passes 9/9, including the browser tests (not skipped here), the hostile-name test and the built-package test. I did not run the full suite or the `html` tests.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
