lue from a missing one. Small change, and it removes a rule that could drift. **Read.**\n\n3. **`deskPage` resolves head and base in four overlapping branches (`server.ts` ~lines 55-80).** The `notice` text is set in three of them. Resolving head first (known, else fallback, with a notice), then base (known, else null with a notice), then computing the default rev would give one flow instead of the `if/else if` chain, which is easy to misread. Medium effort. Keep the existing tests as the check. **Read.**\n\n4. **`route()` is a one-case dispatcher (`server.ts`, the `route` function).** It only checks for `/` and otherwise sends 404. Inlining it into the request handler, with a single `if (url.pathname !== '/')`, removes a name and a call. Small. **Read.**\n\n5. **Two git calls for the default rev (`defaultRev`, `server.ts`).** It runs `rev-list --count` and then `rev-parse`. The count can be skipped by checking `rev-list -n 1 base..head` for output, which stops at the first commit. This only matters for large branches with no commits beyond base, so the benefit is small. **Read; not measured.**\n\nMost of the gain is in items 1 and 2. The rest is clarity.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
