ackground and I'll report its outcome when it finishes. Everything below is from reading the code, not from running it.\n\n**Mismatches**\n\n1. **Summary claims `html` output is unchanged; it isn't.** The summary says \"`html` output and CSP are unchanged\". Groups `sticky-bar` (h17, h20:24-27) and `desk-bar` (h15, h16) edit the shared `src/html/client.js` and `src/html/style.css` that `git gloss html` also embeds. The `html` page now gets a sticky `.top`, a sticky rail at `top: var(--top-h)`, a `ResizeObserver`, and a `measureTop` call. The `sticky-bar` notes admit this (\"same bug, smaller, in `html`\"), so the summary contradicts the author's own group. **Read.**\n\n2. **README is incomplete about the newest-commit fallback.** `docs` (h1) says a branch shows \"its newest commit when there is nothing beyond the base\". `defaultRev` in `src/ary/server.ts` also falls back when the range is above `MAX_RANGE_COMMITS` (200). The `desk-route` notes and the \"choosing a branch far ahead\" test describe that case, but the user-facing docs do not. **Read.**\n\n**Misgraded necessity**\n\n3. **`sticky-bar` is labelled `required`; it looks supporting or incidental.** The task is one document, with no iframe and no second sidebar. Nothing in it requires the top bar to be sticky. The group fixes a layout bug that the author says already exists in `html`, and it adds a `ResizeObserver` plus a `--top-h` variable. The taller bar with wrapping pickers is a reason to fix it here, but that is a supporting need at best. It is also the only group that changes `html` behaviour (finding 1). Suggest relabelling it and splitting out the `html` fix so it can be reviewed on its own.\n\n4. **`remove-shell` is labelled `supporting` for `desk-route`; it is closer to `required`.** The task says to remove the iframe shell and the second sidebar. Deleting `index.html`, `client.js` and `/view` is part of that, not only a follow-on from the new route. Minor.\n\n5. **The \"Back to the default view\" link in `error-page` is incidental.** The author flags it as optional. It is a small addition that an error page does not need to do its job. Removing it costs nothing.\n\n**Removal candidates**\n\n- `sticky-bar` (finding 3): removing it affects only the `html` layout bug and the ary top bar at ≥900px. The `ary` page would still work; the rail might only be partly reachable at scroll 0 when the bar is tall. Defer it, or move it into its own change.\n- The link in `error-page` (finding 5): drop it.\n\n**Simplifications**\n\n- `measureTop` plus `ResizeObserver` could be replaced by a fixed `--top-h` or by a `position: sticky` layout that does not need JS measurement. Only if the sticky change stays.\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n- `build.mjs` now copies `ary/picker.js` and `page.ts` loads it via `asset('../ary/picker.js')`. The path only works in the built `dist/` layout if `page.js` sits one level below `dist/`. The \"built package serves the ary page\" test covers this, but the author did not list it as a risk. **Read.** The test run will confirm it.\n- The author lists \"an empty repo ... gets an error page without pickers\" as a risk. That is correct per `deskPage`, and it is the one place the `ary` page loses its navigation. The error page links only to `/`, which will fail the same way. Not a new bug; the risk is listed.\n\n**Test run**\n\n`npm test` (`node --test 'test/**/*.test.ts'`) was still running when I stopped. I'll report its result when it completes. It will show whether the built-package test and the browser tests pass in this clone.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES\n\nThe full suite passed: 194 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped, exit code 0. That includes the ary, built-package and browser tests, so the browser tests ran rather than being skipped.\n\nThis does not change my earlier findings. The suite passing confirms the code works as the tests describe. It does not address the three issues I raised:\n\n1. **Mismatch (read):** the summary says `html` output is unchanged, but the shared desk CSS and JS change what `git gloss html` produces (sticky top bar, sticky rail, `ResizeObserver`).\n2. **Mismatch (read):** the README says a branch shows its newest commit only \"when there is nothing beyond the base\". The code also falls back when the range exceeds 200 commits.\n3. **Misgrading (read):** `sticky-bar` is labelled `required`, but the task does not need a sticky bar. It fixes a layout bug the author says also exists in `html`, so it should be relabelled and split out.\n\nThe `remove-shell` and \"Back to the default view\" link notes are minor misgrading points from my last report, not failures.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES\n\nThe wait monitor expired without an event. It was only watching for the test summary, which had already come back (194 passed, 0 failed), so nothing is outstanding. The review stands as I reported it: the three issues (summary claim about `html`, the README fallback sentence, and the `sticky-bar` grading) and the verdict `VERDICT: ISSUES`.","verdict":"issues"}
